1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,900
I don't want to go just yet.

2
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:08,300
Before the shuttle launches and I leave this world,

3
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:10,400
there's something I think you ought to know about me.

4
00:00:10,660 --> 00:00:11,680
What is it, Ririko?

5
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:15,060
Everyone wants you to get really good at flirting with spirits

6
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:16,840
so you can make them fall in love with you.

7
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:19,740
And you're supposed to get better by practicing on me.

8
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:20,920
Yeah, that's the plan.

9
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:22,100
What about it?

10
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:24,360
Oh, it's just that I'm afraid.

11
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:27,980
I'm afraid I might be falling in love with you.

12
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:29,920
It's true.

13
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:31,340
We've known each other forever

14
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:33,460
and you've always treated me like a little sister.

15
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:36,780
But do you think you can start looking at me as a woman instead?

16
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:44,200
This is the best day ever!

17
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:48,000
Don't you worry about a thing.

18
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:49,760
I'll even wave to you from Jupiter.

19
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:51,360
It's not super far away.

20
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:53,300
Until next time, big brother.

21
00:00:53,300 --> 00:01:09,160
Spirits.

22
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:12,180
Mysterious girls appearing from another world.

23
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:15,760
Should we fight against their pure strength with weapons of war

24
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:17,700
or should we address them with love?

25
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:21,700
Now, mankind is faced with the ultimate decision.

26
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:42,380
Star Wars

27
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:53,620
So

28
00:01:53,620 --> 00:02:02,840
now

29
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:05,840
LROCK!

30
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:51,860
Dad! Mom!

31
00:02:51,860 --> 00:02:56,740
Murigami!

32
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:20,860
Shen.

33
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:24,860
Yes, Reina?

34
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:40,860
Are you daydreaming again?

35
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:44,860
It's time to implement stage two of your training, so you better be ready.

36
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:46,860
Huh?

37
00:03:46,860 --> 00:03:48,860
This is training?

38
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:50,860
Good afternoon, Shido.

39
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:52,860
Is there something I can help you with?

40
00:03:52,860 --> 00:03:54,860
No, thank you.

41
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:56,860
What do you think you're doing?

42
00:03:56,860 --> 00:04:00,860
Quit wasting everyone's time. Hurry up and make her fall in love with you.

43
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:01,860
Do I have to?

44
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:04,860
You ought to know by now that seducing a spirit is easier said than done.

45
00:04:04,860 --> 00:04:10,860
If you can't even make a human love you, how do you expect to convince a spirit to?

46
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:13,860
You're asking the wrong guy. I'm not a stud.

47
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:16,860
We know. Just throw out a few compliments and see what happens.

48
00:04:16,860 --> 00:04:20,860
If she responds well, we'll give you further instructions.

49
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:23,860
Um, is there something on your mind?

50
00:04:23,860 --> 00:04:26,860
Miss Okamine, that's a cute outfit you're wearing.

51
00:04:26,860 --> 00:04:28,860
What? Goodness, you really think so?

52
00:04:28,860 --> 00:04:30,860
Oh my, that is very flattering of you.

53
00:04:30,860 --> 00:04:32,860
Oh yes, it really does look good.

54
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:36,860
So does your hair and those sexy glasses.

55
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:39,860
Perfect shoes, perfect stockings, perfect attendance book.

56
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:41,860
Shido, is everything all right?

57
00:04:41,860 --> 00:04:44,860
You got way too into that. Stop being creepy on you.

58
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:47,860
I'm kind of busy right now, so I'll see you in class.

59
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:49,860
This can be fixed.

60
00:04:49,860 --> 00:04:53,860
All right, listen closely and do exactly as I say.

61
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:59,860
Here's the truth. I love homeroom. I look forward to going to it every day.

62
00:04:59,860 --> 00:05:02,860
Well, that's nice to hear. I'm so glad that you like it.

63
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:10,860
The main reason is because I get to see you all the time. I can't help it. I think I've fallen in love with you.

64
00:05:10,860 --> 00:05:16,860
Come on, don't say such silly things. Honestly, I'm flattered, but students and teachers can't love each other.

65
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:21,860
No, don't tell me that. I'm dead serious. I want to marry you.

66
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:25,860
You want to marry me?

67
00:05:25,860 --> 00:05:30,860
Is it true? Once you're old enough to get married, I'll be in my 30s. Is that okay?

68
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:33,860
You need to meet my parents. Daddy gets so protected, but I think he'll like you.

69
00:05:33,860 --> 00:05:37,860
He might even give us the house. Once you graduate and get a decent job, I can retire and start having babies.

70
00:05:37,860 --> 00:05:43,860
Huh. We underestimated the enthusiasm of 29-year-old single women. They make for easy targets.

71
00:05:43,860 --> 00:05:46,860
It'll be annoying if she gets more involved than necessary.

72
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:50,860
Hey, Shido, we're done here, so make up some excuses and get out of there pronto.

73
00:05:50,860 --> 00:05:54,860
I'm really sorry, Miss Okamine. I don't think I'm ready for that level of commitment.

74
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:58,860
We can start out in an apartment and work our way up to a three-bedroom condo with a backyard.

75
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:03,860
And don't worry about wedding planning. I've been saving up for 15 years. You can take care of the DJ. I'll do the rest.

76
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:06,860
Could we tell Mo again to say that they get extra special?

77
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:08,860
You found a market with older women. Good to know.

78
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:09,860
Shut up!

79
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:11,860
How can you be so calm when I'm about to get...

80
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:12,860
Ah!

81
00:06:12,860 --> 00:06:14,860
Oh, man. I'm sorry about that.

82
00:06:18,860 --> 00:06:19,860
I'm all right.

83
00:06:19,860 --> 00:06:22,860
Perfect timing. Why don't you practice with her, too?

84
00:06:22,860 --> 00:06:23,860
Huh?

85
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:28,860
She's around the same age as you, so it'll be natural. Plus, even though she's not a spirit, she's a member of the A.S.T.

86
00:06:28,860 --> 00:06:31,860
Doesn't seem like the type to spread rumors, either.

87
00:06:31,860 --> 00:06:33,860
Spread rumors about what?

88
00:06:33,860 --> 00:06:34,860
Just talk to her already!

89
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:41,860
Uh... Hey, Tomichi. Those clothes look nice on you. Where'd you get them?

90
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:43,860
It's a uniform.

91
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:47,860
Come on, idiot. You have to put in more effort than that. Again, with more feeling!

92
00:06:47,860 --> 00:06:48,860
I don't know how.

93
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:50,860
Shin, follow my lead.

94
00:06:51,860 --> 00:06:55,860
To be honest, I already know. I've known all about you for quite a while now.

95
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:56,860
I'm aware of that.

96
00:06:56,860 --> 00:07:03,860
Oh, is that so? Nice. I'm real glad we're in the same class this semester. In fact, I watch you all the time during class when you study.

97
00:07:03,860 --> 00:07:04,860
Yes, likewise.

98
00:07:04,860 --> 00:07:10,860
Is that so? How random. I also like sneaking into your locker after school to sniff your gym clothes.

99
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:11,860
Same here.

100
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:13,860
Okay. I wasn't expecting that.

101
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:14,860
And why not?

102
00:07:14,860 --> 00:07:17,860
Who knew we'd have so much in common, so do you want to go out with me?

103
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:22,860
That came out of nowhere? Don't you think this is a little sudden?

104
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:25,860
I wouldn't mind. I wouldn't mind going out with you.

105
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:30,860
Uh, cool. So, you want to, like, go somewhere with me? Something like that?

106
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:31,860
Like a movie?

107
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:36,860
I'm sorry. I assumed you were asking me out on a date, Shido. Am I wrong?

108
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:38,860
No, not at all. That's exactly what I meant.

109
00:07:38,860 --> 00:07:39,860
Good.

110
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:45,860
Dang it! That's exactly what I meant! How come Reina didn't bail me out of that one? I'm screwed!

111
00:07:45,860 --> 00:07:48,860
What's this?

112
00:07:48,860 --> 00:07:51,860
For you, because you like my uniform.

113
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:52,860
Huh?

114
00:07:52,860 --> 00:07:59,860
Your attention, please. This is not a drill. There have been precursory signs of an impending spatialquake in this vicinity.

115
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:00,860
Please evacuate.

116
00:08:00,860 --> 00:08:02,860
Something just came up. Bye.

117
00:08:02,860 --> 00:08:04,860
Hey, wait a second. Where are you going?

118
00:08:04,860 --> 00:08:08,860
A spatialquake is about to happen. Head back to the Fraxinus for now.

119
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:10,860
Do you think it's a spirit?

120
00:08:10,860 --> 00:08:16,860
Yes, princess. She'll be appearing at your exact location. Rise in high school.

121
00:08:38,860 --> 00:08:46,860
They're on their way now. Roger that.

122
00:08:46,860 --> 00:09:01,860
Here we go. The Quake has started.

123
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:23,860
Consider yourself lucky, Shido. The AST's CR units are deadly, but they weren't built for indoor combat.

124
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:28,860
As long as Princess remains inside the school, the AST will have a hard time interfering with whatever you do.

125
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:30,860
With what I do?

126
00:09:30,860 --> 00:09:33,860
You know exactly what I'm talking about.

127
00:09:33,860 --> 00:09:38,860
Relax. This is what you've been training for the past week. You're as ready as you'll ever be.

128
00:09:38,860 --> 00:09:41,860
You want to save the spirit, or am I wrong?

129
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:47,860
She's right. I don't ever want to see that sad look on her face again.

130
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:51,860
Coterie, you're absolutely sure I can do this?

131
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:58,860
Yes, just believe in yourself. You represent a different way of dealing with the spirits. A more intimate method. Remember that.

132
00:09:58,860 --> 00:10:02,860
Be friendly with them, you sweet talk, and make them fall for me.

133
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:10,860
You're gonna do just fine. Besides, the Fraxinus has got your back.

134
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:14,860
Behold the pride of Rattattusker, ready to respond to any circumstance.

135
00:10:14,860 --> 00:10:20,860
With five marriages and five divorces under his belt, the love master. Bad marriage, go on the way.

136
00:10:20,860 --> 00:10:22,860
Mmm. Hey there.

137
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:26,860
It's the working girl's favorite midnight client.

138
00:10:26,860 --> 00:10:28,860
CEO, Mikimoto.

139
00:10:28,860 --> 00:10:30,860
Who doesn't love love?

140
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:33,860
Go after this lady's fella and you'll regret it.

141
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:35,860
Don't you dare piss her off.

142
00:10:35,860 --> 00:10:37,860
Nail knocker, Shiizaki.

143
00:10:39,860 --> 00:10:42,860
The man with no fewer than a hundred wives.

144
00:10:42,860 --> 00:10:44,860
Dimension breaker, Nakatsugawa.

145
00:10:44,860 --> 00:10:46,860
A-okay.

146
00:10:46,860 --> 00:10:52,860
Lastly, a woman whose love is so strong, not even a silly restraining order can keep her away.

147
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:54,860
Deep love, Minowa!

148
00:10:54,860 --> 00:10:55,860
Okay.

149
00:10:55,860 --> 00:10:57,860
Fantastic. I'm relying on perverts.

150
00:10:57,860 --> 00:10:59,860
Don't worry. Everyone is good at what they do.

151
00:10:59,860 --> 00:11:03,860
And that's only a portion of the troops on our side. Just stay calm.

152
00:11:03,860 --> 00:11:07,860
Even if you die once, you can always start a new game without a penalty.

153
00:11:07,860 --> 00:11:09,860
I'm pretty sure this isn't a game.

154
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:12,860
Have faith in your little sister. Now get in there and flirt!

155
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:41,860
Wait just a minute. I don't want to fight with you. Please, listen to me.

156
00:11:41,860 --> 00:11:45,860
What's your name? And why are you following me?

157
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:46,860
Because...

158
00:11:46,860 --> 00:11:47,860
Don't answer yet!

159
00:11:48,860 --> 00:11:51,860
There has been a change in the mental state of the spirit.

160
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:53,860
Reaction analysis complete.

161
00:11:53,860 --> 00:11:55,860
Displaying choices on screen.

162
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:58,860
My name is Shido Itsuka. I've come to save you.

163
00:11:58,860 --> 00:12:01,860
I'm just a passerby! Please don't kill me!

164
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:05,860
Before asking someone's name, you should give your own.

165
00:12:07,860 --> 00:12:10,860
Well, there they are. Now everyone get to work!

166
00:12:11,860 --> 00:12:15,860
No surprise here. You guys went with the same one I did.

167
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:20,860
The first choice is a tried and true classic, but it doesn't apply in the situation.

168
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:22,860
And it does sound a little cliché.

169
00:12:22,860 --> 00:12:26,860
Option two is also out. If he escapes, he can't continue the conversation.

170
00:12:26,860 --> 00:12:27,860
Number three it is.

171
00:12:27,860 --> 00:12:33,860
I agree. In this case, three makes the most sense. She'll let him live and he'll get to know her better.

172
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:37,860
Okay, Shido, we've made up your mind. Now listen closely and then repeat after me.

173
00:12:37,860 --> 00:12:41,860
What are you waiting for? Answer the question already!

174
00:12:42,860 --> 00:12:44,860
Before asking for someone's name...

175
00:12:44,860 --> 00:12:46,860
You should really give your own first!

176
00:12:46,860 --> 00:12:48,860
I hate you, Yonori!

177
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:52,860
Well, that was unexpected.

178
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:55,860
Unexpected my ass! I could have been dead!

179
00:12:56,860 --> 00:13:00,860
No more time for games. If you do not answer me, I can only assume you are my enemy.

180
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:05,860
My name is Shido Ichika. I'm a student at this school. I've got no reason to bite you!

181
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:10,860
Hold on. This isn't the first time we've crossed paths.

182
00:13:10,860 --> 00:13:13,860
No, it's not. I saw you on the 10th in the city.

183
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:18,860
That's right. I thought so. I remember you saying something odd to me that day.

184
00:13:18,860 --> 00:13:27,860
You said you didn't come to kill me and that you couldn't kill anyone. And now I know that was a lie. Why else would you be here?

185
00:13:29,860 --> 00:13:32,860
Your face. How come you always look so sad?

186
00:13:33,860 --> 00:13:38,860
I'm not trying to do anything. And it's true. I really have no reason to kill you.

187
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:44,860
Quit lying! Every single human is out to get me. I haven't done a thing to them, yet they want me dead.

188
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:45,860
I swear that's not true!

189
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:53,860
You never answered me. You claim to have no intention of killing anyone. If that's really the truth, tell me why it is you came here.

190
00:13:55,860 --> 00:14:00,860
Her first reaction wasn't all that pretty. This time option one's probably the safest choice.

191
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:02,860
I... I wanted to meet you.

192
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:05,860
To meet me? Why would you want that?

193
00:14:08,860 --> 00:14:10,860
Do you guys have any ideas?

194
00:14:10,860 --> 00:14:12,860
I recommend a straightforward approach.

195
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:15,860
Yeah, be clear and direct. This girl's way too dense to get anything subtle.

196
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:20,860
That's a good point. We've already wasted enough time answering all these questions.

197
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:24,860
Uh, it's simple. I came here because I'm interested in you.

198
00:14:24,860 --> 00:14:30,860
I'm in no mood to joke around.

199
00:14:30,860 --> 00:14:32,860
I know. And neither am I.

200
00:14:32,860 --> 00:14:40,860
You want to know the truth? I came here so I could talk to you.

201
00:14:40,860 --> 00:14:46,860
I don't even care what we talk about. Not one bit. You can ignore me if you want to.

202
00:14:46,860 --> 00:14:52,860
But know this. I'm not like every other human. Because...

203
00:14:52,860 --> 00:14:54,860
Stop it! Wait for our signal!

204
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:56,860
Because I'll never let you down!

205
00:14:56,860 --> 00:15:06,860
You said your name was Shido, right? And when you said you were interested in me, were you being serious?

206
00:15:06,860 --> 00:15:07,860
Yes, I was.

207
00:15:07,860 --> 00:15:09,860
But like serious, serious?

208
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:10,860
Serious, serious.

209
00:15:10,860 --> 00:15:13,860
100% serious, serious?

210
00:15:13,860 --> 00:15:16,860
1000% serious, serious!

211
00:15:16,860 --> 00:15:25,860
Jerk! Who would seriously fall for your amateur tricks? Stupid dummy!

212
00:15:25,860 --> 00:15:26,860
But that was from the heart!

213
00:15:26,860 --> 00:15:35,860
Then again, this is different. I still don't know what your intentions are. But you are the only human I've ever had a normal conversation with.

214
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:39,860
You know this world which could serve me well. It might just work.

215
00:15:39,860 --> 00:15:43,860
Yep, it's settled. This should prove your usefulness.

216
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:46,860
Thanks, I guess. Oh yeah, what was your name again?

217
00:15:46,860 --> 00:15:53,860
My name? I've never had one of those. But I suppose I will need one if I want to find out why humans are so awful.

218
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:56,860
Okay, why don't you come up with something you can call me?

219
00:15:56,860 --> 00:15:59,860
Well, she's certainly putting the Fraxness to work, isn't she?

220
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:02,860
Alright crew, we need to think of a name on the double!

221
00:16:05,860 --> 00:16:10,860
The few suggestions we have aren't gonna be enough. Do you want to call in the troops from around the world?

222
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:12,860
One step ahead of you.

223
00:16:13,860 --> 00:16:18,860
Huh? Gosh, now what does she want?

224
00:16:23,860 --> 00:16:26,860
Your wish is my command, my digital darling.

225
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:28,860
Isn't that that fool, Tanamachi?

226
00:16:28,860 --> 00:16:30,860
He's probably sending a dirty text to Shido.

227
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:32,860
That's so lame.

228
00:16:42,860 --> 00:16:45,860
Come on, man! We're not naming Princess after one of your ex-wives!

229
00:16:45,860 --> 00:16:47,860
I don't even know how to pronounce that gibberish!

230
00:16:47,860 --> 00:16:48,860
It's Clarabelle.

231
00:16:48,860 --> 00:16:52,860
The 1920s are over. Can't anyone here think of a halfway decent girl's name?

232
00:16:52,860 --> 00:16:55,860
What about Tomei?

233
00:16:55,860 --> 00:16:58,860
Tomei? Tomei sounds kinda neat, right?

234
00:17:01,860 --> 00:17:03,860
Wow, she's bad. Is Tomei that bad?

235
00:17:03,860 --> 00:17:09,860
Don't think I can't tell what a human is attempting to make fun of me, you got it?

236
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:15,860
